{"title":"Career Roadmap — R&D Engineer","role":"R&D Engineer","summary":"A Polymer/Petrochemical R&D Engineer develops, modifies, tests and commercialises new polymers, plastics, additives, composites, coatings and petrochemical products. The role combines polymer chemistry, chemical engineering, materials science, laboratory experimentation, process engineering and product development.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"Very High — Petrochemical/Plastic/Polymer Engineering provides a strong foundation for R&D in polymers, plastics, petrochemicals, composites and advanced materials."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Polymer science, chemistry, materials, processing, laboratory techniques and experimental research"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"R&D Engineer → Polymer/Product Development Engineer → Senior R&D Engineer"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"R&D Lead, Materials Development Specialist, Product Development Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Principal Scientist/Engineer, R&D Manager, Technology Development Head or Advanced Materials specialist"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Chemistry, mathematics, physics, engineering fundamentals"},{"text":"Understand materials and chemical systems"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Polymer chemistry, thermodynamics, transport phenomena, materials science"},{"text":"Characterise polymer materials"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Polymer processing, composites, additives, testing, formulation"},{"text":"Develop and test polymer formulations"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Product development, advanced materials, research methodology, scale-up"},{"text":"Complete an industry-oriented R&D project"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Scientific Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering mathematics"},{"text":"Engineering chemistry"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Organic chemistry"},{"text":"Basic programming"},{"text":"Engineering drawing"},{"text":"Laboratory safety"},{"text":"Technical communication"},{"text":"Excel/data analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mini-project"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare different polymer materials based on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Density"},{"text":"Tensile strength"},{"text":"Thermal behaviour"},{"text":"Chemical resistance"},{"text":"Cost"},{"text":"Recyclability"},{"text":"Application"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Polymer & Materials Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Polymer chemistry"},{"text":"Polymerisation mechanisms"},{"text":"Molecular weight"},{"text":"Polymer morphology"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Mass transfer"},{"text":"Materials science"},{"text":"Rheology"},{"text":"Polymer characterisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Thermoplastics"},{"text":"Thermosetting polymers"},{"text":"Elastomers"},{"text":"Engineering plastics"},{"text":"High-performance polymers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Characterise a polymer sample and correlate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Processing conditions","Microstructure","Mechanical properties","Final performance"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Processing & Product Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"h","text":"Polymer Processing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Extrusion"},{"text":"Injection moulding"},{"text":"Blow moulding"},{"text":"Compression moulding"},{"text":"Rotational moulding"},{"text":"Thermoforming"},{"text":"Film processing"},{"text":"Fibre processing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Formulation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the purpose of:"},{"t